+++ 1
**Hand Step 5 to the EXEC tier.** With records and decisions settled, and when the EXEC entry names a model that is not an alias of this run's (conventions §10.8) or a depth this run is not already on, and this run is not already `tier=exec`, dispatch a writing `Task` with no `subagent_type`; when EXEC is configured, select named `star-exec` rather than passing a per-call model. It reads this manifest and resumes from Step 5 with `involve=<level> tier=exec` and any valid `auto=unattended` grant. It may not edit EXECPLAN or improvise around a plan-level gap. Re-read EXEC_LOG on return and continue at Step 6; with no usable EXEC override or route, run Step 5 here.
